{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-114866-r4517302","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Apple Pie II","sourcePageId":114866,"sourceRevision":"4517302","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T22:47:57Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Apple%20Pie%20II&oldid=4517302","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:53.744Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for apple pie","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for pie dough","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using apple","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using lard","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using pie dough","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"9ef0af18943df89ba7053d97728a7e9abcbff4e1f5c9177e066444249de79dae","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pie and tart recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Desserts]]\n__NOTOC__\n==Ingredients==\n===Pie crust===\n* 8 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] (225 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) plain [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 4 oz (110 g) [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n* 2 oz (55 g) [[Cookbook:Lard|lard]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] cold water\n===Filling===\n*4 McIntosh [[Cookbook:Apple|apples]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*2 cups [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*3½ tablespoons [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n*[[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] juice (of ½ lemon)\n*½ teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n\n==Procedure==\n===Pie crust===\n#Rub flour, margarine, lard, and salt together until the mixture has the consistency of fine [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|breadcrumbs]].\n#Gently mix in 2 tablespoons water to make a soft but firm dough.\n#Divide dough in half, then roll each half out on floured surface to the size you want your pie.\n#Use one [[Cookbook:Pie Crust|crust]] to line your [[Cookbook:Pie and Tart Pans|pie pan]].\n\n===Filling===\n#Core, peel, and [[Cookbook:Slicing|slice]] the apples into ⅛–¼-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] (0.5–1 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]]) segments.\n#Add lemon juice to the apple segments.\n#Transfer excess juices to the pie pan.\n#Combine the sugar and water in a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]]. Bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] over medium heat, stirring gently until the sugar dissolves and you get a [[Cookbook:Simple Syrup|simple syrup]]. Remove from the heat and let cool until just warm.\n#In a separate bowl, mix the cinnamon, nutmeg, flour, and cornstarch.\n#Combine the apples, spice mixture, and syrup in a bowl. [[Cookbook:Tossing|Toss]] well.\n#Transfer the apple filling to the crust-lined pie pan.\n#Cover the filling with the second pie crust and make three slits on top.\n#Crimp the edges of the crust together, [[Cookbook:Pie Crust Edges|making a decorative border]] if desired.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] in the [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] at 350°[[Cookbook:Fahrenheit|F]] (175°C) for 60 minutes or until golden brown.\n#Take out the pie and let cool.\n#If desired, serve warm with [[Cookbook:Ice Cream|ice cream]], frozen custard, or frozen yogurt.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* You can also use 2 store-bought [[Cookbook:Pie Crust|pie crusts]] instead of making the dough from scratch.\n\n==See also==\n*[[Cookbook:Apple Pie I|Apple Pie I]]\n*[[Cookbook:Apple Pie|Apple Pie]]\n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes for apple pie]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pie dough]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lard]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pie dough]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Apple Pie II","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[],"steps":[],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:114866","recordId":"wikibooks-114866-r4517302","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4517302","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Apple%20Pie%20II&oldid=4517302","sourceSha256":"9ef0af18943df89ba7053d97728a7e9abcbff4e1f5c9177e066444249de79dae","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution